@startuml control_event_acceptance
title Events v2 Control Acceptance and Result Waiting
' Contract baseline: pi-mono-java-design 2ee2a3211da68ad87b0d9cab353e691b00bdaebd
' Java baseline: 808b5a1535316352fbf9c5644c02f717c1be5c2c
' Implementation: c70cc57fb34dafe2acddfd8559a6c90c7a4edf90
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeV2ControlEventService.java#accept
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventStream.java#onClose
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeResultWaitRegistry.java#reserve and bind
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeResultPollingService.java#notifyCommitted
' Pi source: packages/server/src/sessions.ts#LiveSessionManager.executeCommand at 4af9d21d3b4d664e4a29fcabfec85171077248e3
' Observed behavior: Java control acceptance persists a receipt before observing authoritative results.
' Design reason: reserve response capacity before committing a side effect that clients cannot safely replay.
' Java divergence: fixed result waiting across processes is a CampusClaw architecture change.
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
actor "Future HTTP handler" as http
participant "V2 control service" as service
queue "RuntimeEventStream" as stream
participant "Result wait registry" as waits
participant "V2 encoder" as encoder
database "Execution persistence" as persistence
participant "Result polling service" as poller
database "Committed result reader" as reader

http -> service : interrupt or confirmation
service -> stream : create bounded stream
service -> waits : reserve response slot
service -> stream : register one close action
service -> encoder : encode receipt preview
encoder --> service : required data frame
service -> stream : check required capacity
service -> persistence : accept control transaction
persistence --> service : receipt and fixed target
service -> stream : enqueue receipt first
service -> waits : bind target and receipt sequence
service -> poller : notify committed target
poller -> reader : read authoritative results
reader --> poller : committed events and terminal flag
poller -> waits : deliver per response cursor
waits -> stream : enqueue complete events
waits -> stream : complete at terminal
stream -> waits : close reservation once
@enduml
